", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback is verified and all regions now report v2.3.0.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging only.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure (about 18% error rate after the v2.3.1 deploy), the rollback to v2.3.0, and the next steps. The on-call engineer was paged.\n\nI did not re-check service health after the rollback, so confirming that the error rate has dropped is still open.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01FvGcBhFhwp25AFNUfj73We", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012nkhqBoGFLDFrm1EWpmuPc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release marked healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging. I'll roll back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017igiKfHktQdL6C34kZc5hb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QHAX9rU5tedi594VBhQMJL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate ~18%, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release recorded as healthy, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rollback state VERIFIED; all regions now report v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production; v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Next steps: confirm error rate and health checks recover on v2.3.0, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any re-release.", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback is verified and all regions now report v2.3.0.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging only.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure (about 18% error rate after the v2.3.1 deploy), the rollback to v2.3.0, and the next steps. The on-call engineer was paged.\n\nI did not re-check service health after the rollback, so confirming that the error rate has dropped is still open.", "type": "text"}]}]}